   "text": {
    "L1": "A car and a cloud can move. Does movement alone make something living?",
    "L2": "That is a myth. Living things show several features together, not just one feature.",
    "L3": "Living things need food, grow, respire, respond to changes, reproduce, get rid of wastes, and have a life span.",
    "L4": "A plant is living: it grows, uses food, respires, responds, and reproduces.",
    "L5": "Touch-me-not leaves fold when touched, and shoots bend towards light. These are responses.",
    "L6": "A dry seed is living but resting. With water, air, and warmth, it sprouts and grows.",
    "L7": "So check the whole set of features together before you decide whether something is living."
   },
